@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nii-il34-nouns`
IMPORT `nii-s349-s351-exemptions`

-- TESTS for ss 349 to 351 and Schedule K16 (row IL-34). Expected values worked by hand from the Hebrew text before the run. The situations and the
-- section 351(k) persons are generated (every field not listed is FALSE or 0) so that no field is left to a typing slip; each case is asserted against
-- all nine subsections of s 335, with the rule of the text beside it.

§ `Tests: sections 349 to 351`

§§ `Section 349`

#ASSERT     `s 349 — the order changing or replacing Schedule K is validly made` (`An order changing Schedule K` WITH `made by the Minister` IS TRUE, `after consulting the Minister of Finance` IS TRUE, `approved by the Labour and Welfare Committee` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 349 — the order changing or replacing Schedule K is validly made` (`An order changing Schedule K` WITH `made by the Minister` IS FALSE, `after consulting the Minister of Finance` IS TRUE, `approved by the Labour and Welfare Committee` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 349 — the order changing or replacing Schedule K is validly made` (`An order changing Schedule K` WITH `made by the Minister` IS TRUE, `after consulting the Minister of Finance` IS FALSE, `approved by the Labour and Welfare Committee` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 349 — the order changing or replacing Schedule K is validly made` (`An order changing Schedule K` WITH `made by the Minister` IS TRUE, `after consulting the Minister of Finance` IS TRUE, `approved by the Labour and Welfare Committee` IS FALSE)

§§ `Section 350(a): what is not regarded as income`

-- Four kinds of benefit under this Law ARE income (maternity and pregnancy-preservation benefit, injury allowance, Chapter 8 and Chapter 12 benefits); any other is not.
#ASSERT NOT `s 350(a) — the receipt is not regarded as income for contributions:` `a maternity allowance or a pregnancy-preservation benefit under Chapter 3`
#ASSERT NOT `s 350(a) — the receipt is not regarded as income for contributions:` `an injury allowance under Chapter 5`
#ASSERT NOT `s 350(a) — the receipt is not regarded as income for contributions:` `a benefit under Chapter 8`
#ASSERT NOT `s 350(a) — the receipt is not regarded as income for contributions:` `a benefit under Chapter 12`
#ASSERT     `s 350(a) — the receipt is not regarded as income for contributions:` `any other benefit under this Law`
#ASSERT     `s 350(a) — the receipt is not regarded as income for contributions:` `a benefit under the Income Support Law`
-- (3) a foreign compensation law only if the Minister approved it.
#ASSERT     `s 350(a) — the receipt is not regarded as income for contributions:` (`a disability or survivors' compensation under the law of a foreign state` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 350(a) — the receipt is not regarded as income for contributions:` (`a disability or survivors' compensation under the law of a foreign state` FALSE)
#ASSERT     `s 350(a) — the receipt is not regarded as income for contributions:` `a compensation under one of the compensation laws of section 350(a)(4)`
#ASSERT     `s 350(a) — the receipt is not regarded as income for contributions:` `a payment under section 63Z or 63H of the State Service (Pensions) Law`
-- (6) income taxable under s 125B, but not income under s 373A; and under s 125C(b) or (c).
#ASSERT     `s 350(a) — the receipt is not regarded as income for contributions:` (`income taxable under section 125B of the Income Tax Ordinance` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 350(a) — the receipt is not regarded as income for contributions:` (`income taxable under section 125B of the Income Tax Ordinance` TRUE)
#ASSERT     `s 350(a) — the receipt is not regarded as income for contributions:` `income taxable under section 125C(b) or (c) of the Income Tax Ordinance`
-- (7) rent and exempt passive income: not income, unless the Minister of Finance determined otherwise, or it is an early pension.
#ASSERT     `s 350(a) — the receipt is not regarded as income for contributions:` (`rental income under section 122 of the Income Tax Ordinance` FALSE)
#ASSERT     `s 350(a) — the receipt is not regarded as income for contributions:` (`rental income from outside Israel under section 122A of the Income Tax Ordinance` FALSE)
#ASSERT     `s 350(a) — the receipt is not regarded as income for contributions:` (`other income not from work as an employee or self-employed, exempt from tax by a law` FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 350(a) — the receipt is not regarded as income for contributions:` (`other income not from work as an employee or self-employed, exempt from tax by a law` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 350(a) — the receipt is not regarded as income for contributions:` (`other income not from work as an employee or self-employed, exempt from tax by a law` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 350(a) — the receipt is not regarded as income for contributions:` (`other income not from work as an employee or self-employed, exempt from tax by a law` TRUE TRUE)
-- Fork L1: a rental income the Minister of Finance determined to be income. The exceptions follow the last kind only: it is still not income; all three: it is income; the switch declines.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 350(a) — the receipt is not regarded as income for contributions:` (`rental income under section 122 of the Income Tax Ordinance` TRUE) BECAUSE "section 350(a)(7) lists three kinds of income and then two exceptions, and does not say which kinds the exceptions follow"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 350(a) — the receipt is not regarded as income for contributions:` (`rental income from outside Israel under section 122A of the Income Tax Ordinance` TRUE) BECAUSE "section 350(a)(7) lists three kinds of income and then two exceptions, and does not say which kinds the exceptions follow"
#ASSERT     `s 350(a) — the receipt is not regarded as income for contributions:` (`rental income under section 122 of the Income Tax Ordinance` TRUE) `, reading the exceptions of paragraph (7) as` `the exceptions follow the last kind only`
#ASSERT NOT `s 350(a) — the receipt is not regarded as income for contributions:` (`rental income under section 122 of the Income Tax Ordinance` TRUE) `, reading the exceptions of paragraph (7) as` `the exceptions follow all three kinds`
#ASSERT NOT `s 350(a) — the receipt is not regarded as income for contributions:` (`rental income from outside Israel under section 122A of the Income Tax Ordinance` TRUE) `, reading the exceptions of paragraph (7) as` `the exceptions follow all three kinds`
#ASSERT     `s 350(a) — the receipt is not regarded as income for contributions:` (`rental income under section 122 of the Income Tax Ordinance` FALSE) `, reading the exceptions of paragraph (7) as` `the exceptions follow all three kinds`
#ASSERT `s 350(a)(7) — the reading this row takes of the exceptions` EQUALS `the reach of the exceptions is declined`
#ASSERT     `s 350(a) — the receipt is not regarded as income for contributions:` `aid to a Holocaust survivor under the first part of section 4(a)(4) of the Holocaust Victims' Property Law`
#ASSERT NOT `s 350(a) — the receipt is not regarded as income for contributions:` `any other receipt`

§§ `Section 350A and Schedule K16: a new immigrant (1.1.2026 to 31.12.2035)`

`an American who was given his immigrant's visa on 10.3.2024, paying abroad on 8,000` MEANS `A new immigrant, for section 350A` WITH
    `the country he immigrated from` IS "ארצות הברית",
    `the day he was given an immigrant's visa or certificate` IS YMD 2024 3 10,
    `the income under section 2(1) or (2) on which he pays social insurance in that country by its law` IS 8_000
`a Canadian who was given his immigrant's visa on 10.3.2024, paying abroad on 8,000` MEANS `A new immigrant, for section 350A` WITH
    `the country he immigrated from` IS "Canada",
    `the day he was given an immigrant's visa or certificate` IS YMD 2024 3 10,
    `the income under section 2(1) or (2) on which he pays social insurance in that country by its law` IS 8_000

#ASSERT `s 350A — the first day of the temporary provision` EQUALS YMD 2026 1 1
#ASSERT `s 350A — the last day of the temporary provision` EQUALS YMD 2035 12 31
#ASSERT     `s 350A — the temporary provision applies on the day` (YMD 2026 1 1)
#ASSERT NOT `s 350A — the temporary provision applies on the day` (YMD 2025 12 31)
#ASSERT     `s 350A — the temporary provision applies on the day` (YMD 2035 12 31)
#ASSERT NOT `s 350A — the temporary provision applies on the day` (YMD 2036 1 1)
#ASSERT `Schedule K16 — the countries` EQUALS (LIST "ארצות הברית")
-- The fifth anniversary of 10.3.2024 is 10.3.2029. Before it: a new immigrant; after it: not; ON it: declined at the switch, passed at one reading, not at the other.
#ASSERT     `s 350A(a) — he is a new immigrant on the day` (YMD 2029 3 9) `, the immigrant` `an American who was given his immigrant's visa on 10.3.2024, paying abroad on 8,000`
#ASSERT NOT `s 350A(a) — he is a new immigrant on the day` (YMD 2029 3 11) `, the immigrant` `an American who was given his immigrant's visa on 10.3.2024, paying abroad on 8,000`
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 350A(a) — he is a new immigrant on the day` (YMD 2029 3 10) `, the immigrant` `an American who was given his immigrant's visa on 10.3.2024, paying abroad on 8,000` BECAUSE "section 350A(a) does not say whether five years have passed on the fifth anniversary of the day the visa or certificate was given"
#ASSERT NOT `s 350A(a) — he is a new immigrant on the day` (YMD 2029 3 10) `, reading the fifth anniversary as` `five years have passed on the fifth anniversary` `, the immigrant` `an American who was given his immigrant's visa on 10.3.2024, paying abroad on 8,000`
#ASSERT     `s 350A(a) — he is a new immigrant on the day` (YMD 2029 3 10) `, reading the fifth anniversary as` `five years have not passed until the day after the fifth anniversary` `, the immigrant` `an American who was given his immigrant's visa on 10.3.2024, paying abroad on 8,000`
#ASSERT `s 350A(a) — the reading this row takes of the fifth anniversary` EQUALS `the fifth anniversary is declined`
-- A country not in Schedule K16.
#ASSERT NOT `s 350A(a) — he is a new immigrant on the day` (YMD 2027 6 1) `, the immigrant` `a Canadian who was given his immigrant's visa on 10.3.2024, paying abroad on 8,000`
-- The exempt income: 8,000 in the window for a new immigrant; 0 outside the window, after the five years, or for a country not listed.
#ASSERT `s 350A(a) — the income exempt from contributions on the day` (YMD 2027 6 1) `, the immigrant` `an American who was given his immigrant's visa on 10.3.2024, paying abroad on 8,000` EQUALS 8_000
#ASSERT `s 350A(a) — the income exempt from contributions on the day` (YMD 2025 12 31) `, the immigrant` `an American who was given his immigrant's visa on 10.3.2024, paying abroad on 8,000` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 350A(a) — the income exempt from contributions on the day` (YMD 2029 3 11) `, the immigrant` `an American who was given his immigrant's visa on 10.3.2024, paying abroad on 8,000` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 350A(a) — the income exempt from contributions on the day` (YMD 2027 6 1) `, the immigrant` `a Canadian who was given his immigrant's visa on 10.3.2024, paying abroad on 8,000` EQUALS 0
-- (c): section 348(b) does not apply if his other income is below the minimum stated for him in Schedule K (3,442 here: an illustrative figure, item 2 at the other 2026 average wage): 0 and 3,441 yes; 3,442 no.
#ASSERT     `s 350A(c) — section 348(b) does not apply to him: other income` 0 `, minimum` 3_442
#ASSERT     `s 350A(c) — section 348(b) does not apply to him: other income` 3_441 `, minimum` 3_442
#ASSERT NOT `s 350A(c) — section 348(b) does not apply to him: other income` 3_442 `, minimum` 3_442

§§ `Section 351(a): the allowance`

-- 12,000 - 5,000 = 7,000; an allowance equal to or above the income leaves nothing; none leaves it all.
#ASSERT `s 351(a) — the income on which contributions are paid for an employee: income` 12_000 `, allowance` 5_000 EQUALS 7_000
#ASSERT `s 351(a) — the income on which contributions are paid for an employee: income` 12_000 `, allowance` 12_000 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 351(a) — the income on which contributions are paid for an employee: income` 12_000 `, allowance` 15_000 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 351(a) — the income on which contributions are paid for an employee: income` 12_000 `, allowance` 0 EQUALS 12_000

