§§ `Section 351: which subsections of section 335 fall away for him`

-- Each case against all nine subsections. The hand rules (the text of s 351):
-- (b) an old-age pension is due, or the age 70 / Part D age is reached: 335(b), (e), (g), (h), (i).
-- (c) neither employee nor self-employed, at retirement age, no pension yet: the same five.
-- (d) first limb: a Chapter 5 or 9 disability pension and no other income: no contributions at all. (d) second limb: a stable disability pension (ss 105, 200) or an unstable one
--     fixed for a year at least (s 200), even with other income: 335(a), (b), (d), (e), (g), (h), (i).
-- (f), (g), (g1), (k): no contributions at all (with the conditions of each). (h), (i), (j): 335(d), 335(g), 335(h) for a woman insured under Chapter 6, 9, 10 and a housewife or pensioned widow.

