§§ `Fixtures: persons who may be exempt under section 351(k)`

`k: a benefit received` MEANS `A person who may be exempt under section 351(k)` WITH
    `he is neither an employee nor self-employed` IS TRUE,
    `his income in the period does not exceed the Schedule K item 3 minimum` IS TRUE,
    `he receives a benefit or compensation named in section 350 other than unemployment benefit for a full month` IS TRUE,
    `he is a disabled person entitled to a Chapter 9 disability pension, in a period beginning on the determining date of section 195` IS FALSE,
    `he immigrated under the Law of Return or holds a permanent or A/5 visa and was given an absorption basket` IS FALSE,
    `the months from the day he immigrated or entered to the end of the period asked about` IS 0,
    `his age in whole years` IS 0,
    `he is a secondary-school student, in vocational training, in a pre-military preparatory programme or a volunteer in a service year` IS FALSE,
    `he began regular service, national service or community volunteering before he was 21` IS FALSE,
    `he is insured under Chapter 11` IS FALSE,
    `the months the exemption will have run by the end of the period asked about` IS 0,
    `he finished regular service other than on a career commitment, serving two thirds of the duty period and not discharged for unfitness with grave misconduct, or was discharged for health or disability` IS FALSE,
    `he finished national-civic service or volunteering, serving two years or ending it by an injury during and because of it` IS FALSE,
    `the months from the end of his service to the end of the period asked about` IS 0,
    `the Minister set an exemption for him by rules` IS FALSE

